# tasks_objects_private: A private buffer is a copy, and a synchronize copies it out only when it needs one (Resource::needs_sync): guest-invalid and host-valid (section 4.10). In turn: a fill with the invalidate-host flag (the guest's contents are copied in first); SynchronizeResources (53); the guest rewrites its copy and InvalidateResources (52) marks the host copy stale before a fill and a synchronize; a fill with the synchronize flag; a fill with the invalidate-guest flag, after which SynchronizeAndDiscardResources (62) copies out every fill so far; a fill, DiscardResources (63) and 53; 52 setting host-valid and clearing guest-valid, then 53, which copies again. In-process, nothing reaches the guest page before the invalidate-guest fill. In the service a private buffer is a Shared detach buffer, so each fill lands at once (section 6.10). The guest page is dumped after each.
